WEBVTT

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.190
My beloved people,

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.030
heed me, as I share with you the words of our Emperor.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.590
It has been decided...

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.290
that our nation of Yamato shall invade Tusukuru!

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.000
Still...

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.250
Just had to be there, huh?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.320
Don't say that.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.500
This is the will of the Emperor.{rip Azir passive}

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.450
That's right.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:45.770
They might be beyond our comprehension, 
but I'm certain the Emperor has his reasons.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.690
B-But...

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.890
When I think about how Kuon-sama must feel...

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.150
That's true, but...

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.820
My lord...

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.420
Have some hot, freshly made tea.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.100
Have you seen Kuon?

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.590
I see.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.960
Where is Big Sister?

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.590
I-Is she still in her room?

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:34.490
Yeah.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.940
I'll take a peek, see if she's okay.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:37.930
I'll go, too.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:38.940
Wait.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.350
You know what's going on.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.370
Give her some space for now.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.610
Hey, it's war!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.660
We're invading Tusukuru!

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.480
Shinonon!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.800
You're being too loud!

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.560
Latest news!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.910
Yamato's forces have successfully 
pushed deep into Tusukuru territory

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.900
and seized one of their strongholds!

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:10.930
If you want to know more, 
buy a copy and read at your leisure!

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:23.680
Come in.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.270
What is it today?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.270
Not cleaning more gutters, I hope!

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.100
That smell is just, you know...

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.770
The invading forces in Tusukuru are struggling.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.890
We'd anticipated opposition, but not to this extent.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.530
We sent Yamato's finest armies,

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.670
but each general has their own way of thinking,

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.220
and their own way of fighting.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.150
Thus, at times they struggle to cooperate.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.350
And it appears the enemy has used that to their advantage.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.940
The enemy knows us all too well.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.580
It seems we've underestimated them.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:20.670
Even General Munechika is struggling.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.380
How's she doing?

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.810
There's no real cause for concern.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.920
This war remains a stalemate,

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:33.660
and she's making every effort possible to keep her army under control.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:41.250
But even in the advent of success, her situation is far from ideal.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.300
Their supply lines have been cut, 
and they're isolated.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.450
It's only a matter of time before their resources run dry.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:55.950
Yeah, but we're not just going to sit back and let that happen, right?

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.710
There's a reason we can't let it.{which is???? can't edit this shit if he's being so vague}{Every generals are busy with their own thing, so they can't send any supplies}

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:05.640
If we are to rely on sheer strength, 
Vurai would be most appropriate.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:10.220
However, Vurai has left to 
quell a barbarian uprising.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:10.900
Then...

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:15.800
<i>I</i> have been tasked with defending the capital in Munechika's place.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.180
The other Pillar Generals have tasks of their own,

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:21.600
and are unable to depart at this time.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.900
So what do you want me to do?

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:28.780
Master Haku...

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:35.160
I want you to deliver supplies to the invading forces in Tusukuru.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:42.160
Simultaneously, I want you to aid Kiuru, who went with the reinforcements.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:44.380
Kiuru?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:50.970
Kiuru has gone to deliver supplies as envoy of the Ennakamui Ouro.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.990
Will you accept?

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:01.640
Oshutoru...

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.100
You know what you're asking me to do, right?

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:15.200
You're telling me to participate in the invasion of Tusukuru.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.450
I am well aware.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.790
The supplies leave in the morning.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:26.960
There is no one else who can do it.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:34.720
Fine.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:38.350
I accept.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.980
Forgive me.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.460
Hey, Mommy!

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.020
What's for dinner today?

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:55.990
Well...

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:57.340
What do you think it is?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:57.990
Hmm...

00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:59.540
Amamunii!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:00.990
Nope.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.280
Okay, let's go home.

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:03.790
Yeah.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.010
Daddy's waiting.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.000
Okay!

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.580
Hey!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.560
Is that some kind of ritual?

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:53.400
We're tryin'a cheer Kuon-han up.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:10:00.160
But that ain't possible till she comes crawlin' outta that room o' hers.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.750
So we're trying to lure her out with the smell of her favorite food.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.550
Oh yeah, mister...

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.560
Didn't Oshutoru-han wanna see you today?

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:13.570
Did he have a new job for you?

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.290
Yeah, about that...

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.620
Kuon, I have something to tell you.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:36.840
Oshutoru says the Tusukuru invasion force is in danger.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:40.310
They're isolated and their 
supply lines have been cut.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:41.880
And...

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:46.130
they're going to run out of 
supplies eventually, he says.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.980
Seems Tusukuru knows the art of war well...

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:54.000
So here's the thing.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:59.150
He asked me to deliver supplies.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.660
Tomorrow morning, no less.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:11.250
To be honest, I think I'm more suited to cleaning gutters.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.990
But I'm worried about Munechika,

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.260
and I want to help Kiuru.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:21.810
And Oshutoru...

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.760
Well, how to say it...

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:31.770
So I've decided to carry out his request.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:37.770
I'm just going to keep doing as much as I can, same as always, though.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:43.520
Kuon, I've told you what's going on.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.280
But I'm heading to war.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.790
I don't know what'll happen.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:55.290
It may mean fighting the people of your 
homeland, whom I know you love deeply.

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.230
So...

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.800
So I'm...

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.550
leaving you here.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:04.300
I'm not taking you with me.

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:06.550
You understand, right, Kuon?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.060
Kuon...

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:15.810
I know you can hear me, Kuon!

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.730
Come on, say something, Kuon!

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.950
What's going on?

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.570
Kuon-sama...

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:37.780
Big Sis left a while ago.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.340
What will you do?

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:46.970
Well, I'm tired now, so...

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:48.560
Follow her!

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.600
Tell her! You have to!

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.080
Hear, hear!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.390
You can't just back down after sayin' all that!

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:58.100
A good man sees things through to the end.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.410
H-Haku-sama...

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.610
Please take care of Kuon-sama.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.210
But I don't really...

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.510
Rightio, I think it's time to pack.{I just realized that he talks like a woman now thatI hear more line from him}

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.860
Me, too.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:11.370
At once!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.620
Why?

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.440
Your fault for sayin' we leave tomorrow, mister!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.110
There's no time to waste.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:21.490
Hey!

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:23.700
Truly, how like you, Haku-san.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:27.000
To volunteer for that which others will not...

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.260
How did this happen?

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.530
This one's for Haku-sama.

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:38.980
This one's for Kokopo.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.840
Kuon-sama...

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:04.280
U-Um...

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:24.560
The supplies have already been loaded onto a ship at the port.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.270
A sh-ship?

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:31.510
We're going to resupply in Shahhoro and then head to Tusukuru.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:32.630
Shahhoro?

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.560
That's your homeland, isn't it, Atui-sama?

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:40.720
If this were any other kinda trip, 
I'd love to take you 'round for some sightseein'.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.140
Real pity, actually.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.650
We'll just have to wait until we're at peace again.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.350
Th-That's right...

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:49.900
We'll just hold off on it until then.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.700
I want to go with Kuon-sama and everyone else, right?

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.190
Be lookin' forward to it!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:06.670
The sea... Boats... Waves...

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.690
Finished at last, are we?

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:21.180
Truly, that was quite a load.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.690
You didn't do a damned thing, did you?

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:28.530
Excellent work.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.760
Did you find her?

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:51.850
Well, no, I...

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:54.260
I wasn't expecting any different, but...

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:56.220
Did you go to the kebab stall?

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.160
O-Of course.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.030
The noodle shop?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:16:59.970
Like I'd miss that place!

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:01.500
What about...

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.760
Listen, I'm just about to...

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:04.810
Haku-sama!

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.070
Rurutie?

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:07.970
What's wrong?

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:14.070
I made some snacks for 
everyone to eat on the way.

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.740
Could you try one please?

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.740
No, I'm a little busy for stuff like that.

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.450
"Stuff like that"...

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.850
No, uh, I didn't mean it that way...

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:26.560
Mister!

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.270
Good timing.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.750
Not you guys as well...

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:36.560
Nosuri-han ain't makin' any sense!

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:41.330
I'm asking her how not to get seasick.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.520
O-Of course, I'm not asking for my own sake!

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.450
A good woman doesn't get seasick, you know!

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.680
What's this here "seasick" mean?

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.190
Y-You don't know?

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.670
When you get sick at sea!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:58.810
You get dizzy!

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.460
You feel terrible.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.530
Like that.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:05.430
Of course, that was all hearsay!

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.040
Mister!

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:09.680
What a pain.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:12.040
Just have Kuon make you some medicine.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:17.300
All right, I'm busy, so...

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:18.900
Haku? Is Haku present?

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:21.410
Oh, give me a break.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.180
Ah! Haku!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.520
What is it?

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:29.510
I want you to deliver this to Munechika.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:30.690
What is it?

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:32.090
That is confidential!

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:38.690
Needless to say, this is an item that will raise her morale.

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:41.950
But you <i>must not</i> open it.

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.350
Right, right...

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:44.950
Here.

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:46.950
O-Okay...

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:48.520
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:49.450
Wait!

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:52.170
I'm not done yet!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.380
I don't get it.

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:12.850
What seems to be the matter?

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:14.110
Oh, nothing.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:23.360
Um...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.620
So like...

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:32.830
He tries to make me work!

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.210
That bastard...

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.630
Are you listening?

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:39.540
I don't wanna work, damn it!

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:46.550
Cleaning this gutter. Cleaning that gutter. 
 Cleaning every damned gutter...

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:50.190
I finally get someone to do my dirty work and he disappears.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:52.890
I'm so sick of this.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:20:00.150
Why are there always more and more people?

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:05.930
Why do I get fewer and fewer kebabs?

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:11.660
Even though more people come,
 I still have to clean the gutters myself.

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:13.860
Why, damn it!?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:20.080
Why does all this stuff keep happening to me?

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:24.020
I get attacked, I almost drown...

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:28.450
The shitty stuff always happens to me...

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.470
Y'know, I...

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.920
I... just wanna... break...

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:50.100
Please, remain by her side,

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:52.450
come what may.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:30.660
Ow!

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:43.920
Sorry!

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:47.170
I overslept—
